{
  "airbags-and-seat-belts-are-import-heavy": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Teen_fastening_seat_belt.jpg/960px-Teen_fastening_seat_belt.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Teenager fastening a car seat belt\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Seat belt webbing sits inside one of the most import-dependent categories in India's automotive textiles, even as safety-systems majors localise assembly. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teen_fastening_seat_belt.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Teen fastening seat belt</a>, State Farm, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "announced-vs-delivered-three-indian": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Optima_Plus_%28Hero_Electric%2C_India%29.jpg/960px-Optima_Plus_%28Hero_Electric%2C_India%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Hero Electric Optima Plus electric scooter in India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Electric two-wheelers like this one are what state EV subsidy portals such as UP's actually approve applications for — the after-numbers this piece checks against the policy targets. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Optima_Plus_(Hero_Electric,_India).jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Optima Plus (Hero Electric, India)</a>, Viswaprabha, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "basf-and-mitsubishi-are-running": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Flooded_paddy_field_Raichur_Karnataka_India_monsoon_irrigation_July_2025.jpg/960px-Flooded_paddy_field_Raichur_Karnataka_India_monsoon_irrigation_July_2025.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Flooded rice paddy field in Raichur, Karnataka, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Flooded paddies like this one are the methane source that rice carbon-credit programmes — including the separate BASF and Mitsubishi efforts this piece untangles — are built to reduce. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flooded_paddy_field_Raichur_Karnataka_India_monsoon_irrigation_July_2025.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Flooded paddy field Raichur Karnataka India monsoon irrigation July 2025</a>, Vraj Acharya, WELL Labs, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "below-250-is-where-real-junk-lives": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/BSE_-_Bombay_Stock_Exchange_Building.jpg/960px-BSE_-_Bombay_Stock_Exchange_Building.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Bombay Stock Exchange building in Mumbai\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The Bombay Stock Exchange, one of the two exchanges whose sub-₹250 stocks this piece isolates from the wider under-₹1,000 bucket that averaged their risk away. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BSE_-_Bombay_Stock_Exchange_Building.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BSE - Bombay Stock Exchange Building</a>, Niyantha Shekhar, CC BY 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "beyond-pump-what-upi-fee-would-cost": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Bhim_upi_ID_to_accept_entrance_fee_at_Shaurya_Smarak_Bhopal.jpg/960px-Bhim_upi_ID_to_accept_entrance_fee_at_Shaurya_Smarak_Bhopal.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"BHIM UPI QR code payment sign in India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">A BHIM UPI QR code of the kind now standing at counters across every merchant category this piece runs the post-MDR fee arithmetic against — groceries, restaurants and fuel alike. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhim_upi_ID_to_accept_entrance_fee_at_Shaurya_Smarak_Bhopal.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bhim upi ID to accept entrance fee at Shaurya Smarak Bhopal</a>, Suyash.dwivedi, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "blending-on-budget-energy-density-and": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Petrol_pump%2C_Nagpur%2C_India.jpg/960px-Petrol_pump%2C_Nagpur%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Petrol pump in Nagpur, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Fuel dispensed at pumps like this one already carries India's ethanol-in-petrol mandate — one of the four blend pairs this piece measures for energy-density loss. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petrol_pump,_Nagpur,_India.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Petrol pump, Nagpur, India</a>, Ganesh Dhamodkar, CC BY 1.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "can-rupee-trade-actually-offset": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Tower_and_building_of_Reserve_Bank_of_India%2C_Mumbai_02.jpg/960px-Tower_and_building_of_Reserve_Bank_of_India%2C_Mumbai_02.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Reserve Bank of India tower building in Mumbai\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The Reserve Bank of India, whose Vostro-account infrastructure sits underneath the rupee-trade-settlement question this piece checks against real oil and Russia-trade data. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tower_and_building_of_Reserve_Bank_of_India,_Mumbai_02.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tower and building of Reserve Bank of India, Mumbai 02</a>, Pinakpani, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "cgd-geographical-areas-district": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/CNG_filling_station%2C_Delhi.JPG/960px-CNG_filling_station%2C_Delhi.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"CNG filling station in Delhi\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">A CNG filling station of the kind served by the City Gas Distribution geographical areas this piece maps district by district, bidding round by bidding round. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CNG_filling_station,_Delhi.JPG\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CNG filling station, Delhi</a>, Subhashish Panigrahi, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "cheap-yen-rupee-roads-where-carry-trade": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Ahmedabad%E2%80%93Vadodara_National_Expressway_1%2C_Gujarat%2C_India_%282020%29.jpg/960px-Ahmedabad%E2%80%93Vadodara_National_Expressway_1%2C_Gujarat%2C_India_%282020%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"Ahmedabad–Vadodara National Expressway in Gujarat, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">Indian infrastructure like this expressway is exactly what yen-denominated loans from JBIC and Japanese lenders help finance — the carry-trade arithmetic this piece checks against real deals. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmedabad%E2%80%93Vadodara_National_Expressway_1,_Gujarat,_India_(2020).jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ahmedabad–Vadodara National Expressway 1, Gujarat, India (2020)</a>, Naveen Ranjan Giri, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  },
  "chemical-import-substitution-analysis": {
    "picture_html": "<figure style=\"margin:1.6rem 0\">\n<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/OPaL_Dahej_Project_Panorama_View.jpg/960px-OPaL_Dahej_Project_Panorama_View.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=imageinfo&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" alt=\"OPaL petrochemical complex at Dahej, India\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;display:block\"/>\n<figcaption class=\"gb-note\" style=\"margin-top:.4rem\">The OPaL petrochemical complex at Dahej makes exactly the products this piece re-derives import figures for — ethylene, polyethylene and polypropylene. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OPaL_Dahej_Project_Panorama_View.jpg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OPaL Dahej Project Panorama View</a>, Rajiv Nair EIL, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
  }
}